  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACTION FOR INCLUSIVE, TRANSPARENT AND ACCOUNTABLE BUDGET SYSTEM FOR EFFECTIVE SERVICE DELIVERY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone, over the years, has enacted several laws and formulated policies that are geared towards promoting the aspects of public accountability, public transparency and public participation in Public Financial Management (PFM) issues. Implementation has, however, been a challenge which is affecting the quality services delivered in the country. 
Instances are that: little has been achieved in the area of Audit Accountability. Lots of recommendations, the Auditor General&#x2019;s Reports have preferred over the years, which the MDAs have not complied with. These include following laid-down processes and procedures in procurements, for which the rules are clear in terms of how the various procurements should be carried out. Some MDAs could not provide proper supporting documents to show proof of expenditure when the documents are required for auditing purposes. The Auditors have found over time, material misstatements and or overstatements, when thorough examinations are done on the available fiscal and administrative documents that are available for audit inspection. This mostly affects the quality of Audit Opinions; the Auditor General have made over the period. Cash losses and other service delivery issues, have been growing over time and this is becoming worrisome for how Audit Accountability can be enhanced, both at the Central and Local Council levels.</narrative>
  </description>
